{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And these are the kings who reigned in the land of Edom</b>. This was written to declare that the blessing of Isaac was fulfilled in him, for he said to him, \"and by your sword you shall live\" (Genesis 27:40), since they overpowered the sons of Seir the Horite and reigned over them in their land. And these cities are provinces in the land of Edom, for Bozrah belongs to Edom, as it is written (Isaiah 34:6), \"For HaShem has a sacrifice in Bozrah, and a great slaughter in the land of Edom,\" and likewise the land of the Temanite is from Edom, as is said of it (Obadiah 1:9), \"And your mighty men, O Teman, shall be dismayed, so that every man may be cut off from the mount of Esau,\" and all of them are likewise. But Scripture relates that no king was the son of a king, as they were in Israel. And <b>before any king reigned</b> — many days before; the meaning of \"before any king reigned\" is not that the rule of these extended until the kingship of Israel (see Rashi and Radak), but rather to say that then they would no longer have a kingdom, to fulfill \"and your brother you shall serve\" (Genesis 27:40). And it is possible that all of these had already passed away in the days of Moses, for they were old men at the time they were made kings and did not live long."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:22:00.622327056Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}